{"tid": "num-049", "family": "integer arithmetic and number theory (digits, divisors, gcd, primes, base conversion)", "spec": "Convert a non-negative integer n into its lowercase hexadecimal representation as a string, with no leading zeros or prefix (except that 0 itself maps to \"0\").", "signature": "def int_to_hex_string(n):", "visible_tests": ["assert int_to_hex_string(255) == 'ff'", "assert int_to_hex_string(26) == '1a'", "assert int_to_hex_string(0) == '0'"], "hidden_tests": ["assert int_to_hex_string(1) == '1'", "assert int_to_hex_string(16) == '10'", "assert int_to_hex_string(256) == '100'", "assert int_to_hex_string(1000) == '3e8'", "assert int_to_hex_string(65535) == 'ffff'", "assert int_to_hex_string(4095) == 'fff'", "assert int_to_hex_string(4096) == '1000'", "assert int_to_hex_string(10) == 'a'", "assert int_to_hex_string(15) == 'f'", "assert int_to_hex_string(100) == '64'", "assert int_to_hex_string(999) == '3e7'", "assert int_to_hex_string(2748) == 'abc'", "assert int_to_hex_string(3735928559) == 'deadbeef'", "assert int_to_hex_string(31) == '1f'", "assert int_to_hex_string(64) == '40'", "assert int_to_hex_string(128) == '80'"], "reference": "def int_to_hex_string(n):\n    if n == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n    return format(n, 'x')"}
